Description: Periodic NFS to Azure Blob sync via rclone
 Hardened, idempotent one-shot sync from an NFS mount to an Azure Blob
 container using rclone. Ships systemd .service and .timer units, a
 benchmark helper, and a sample rclone configuration.
 .
 Designed for high-volume NFS workloads on the order of 1M+ files. The
 periodic timer runs as a dedicated system user (nfs-sync), with
 flock-based overlap protection and quiescence filtering to avoid
 uploading files that are still being written.
 .
 Run nfs-sync-bench(1) to assess feasibility before enabling the timer.
